ps of width 5/6 with values >15 -> base32/base64 INDEX;  ䷀.. hexagrams -> base64;  only space/TAB -> bits\n dotted quads / #RRGGBB / 4e69:6365 . IPv4 / colour / IPv6 bytes;  base64-ish that won't decode -> undo rev/rot13/atbash 1st (U4fV = rot13 H4sI)\n only A D F G X (V) -> ADFGX/ADFGVX (key: title word + crib);  only A C G T -> DNA 2-bit / codon\n %XX .............................. URL (D7);  &#..; -> HTML (D8);  \\uXXXX -> JSON (D9);  \\xNN -> C escape\n U+XXXX / %uXXXX / \\U0000XXXX -> chr(int(h,16));  =XX / soft \"=\\n\" -> quoted-printable;  =?UTF-8?B?..?= -> MIME\n A-Z2-7 (=) ....................... base32 (D10);  0-9A-V -> base32hex;  ybndrfg8.. -> z-base-32;  no ILOU -> Crockford\n A-Za-z0-9+/ (=), len%4==0 ........ base64 (D1); H4sI = GZIP inside (D21: base64 -d | gzip -dc); eJ zlib, Qlpo bz2,\n                                    /Td6WFo xz, KLUv/ zstd, UEsDB zip, N3q8 7z; bytes binary -> sniff magic, never score\n A-Za-z0-9-_ no = ................. base64url (D11);  [0-9A-Za-z] only, no pad -> base62 (x1.34) / base36 one case (x1.55)\n no 0 O I l + / = ................. base58 (x1.37)\n 0-9A-Z plus space $%*+-./: ....... base45 (x1.5)\n ! .. u (+z), maybe <~ ~> ......... ascii85;  RFC1924 set (no quotes , . / : [ \\ ]) -> base85; .-:+=^!/*?&<>()[]{}@%$# -> Z85\n ~all printable, no ' - \\ ......... basE91 (x1.23);  ! .. } minus \" ` -> base92\n begin 644 / lines start M or h ... uuencode / xxencode;  xn-- labels -> punycode/IDNA\nNON-ASCII:\n U+2800-28FF ⠝⠊⠉⠑ ................. Braille (⠼ = number sign)\n fullwidth Ｎｉｃｅ / math 𝐍𝐢𝐜𝐞 / ⓝ .. NFKC normalize\n ɐ q ɔ p ǝ ɟ ƃ ɥ ᴉ ʞ ɯ ɹ ʇ ʌ ʍ ʎ ...... upside-down (chepy from_upside_down, then maybe [::-1])\n CJK U+7Cxx, spaces kept -> ROT8000;  dense CJK/Hangul -> base65536/2048;  emoji 1/byte -> base100;  CJK U+xx00 -> swap bytes\n invisible U+200B/C/D/2060/FEFF -> zero-width stego;  ASCII-looking with odd bytes -> homoglyphs (Cyrillic)\nSAME LENGTH, LETTERS ONLY CHANGE (word lengths 4 4 8 4 6! ... kept):\n best rot-N English ............... Caesar (D2 rot13, D14 +7); digits also shifted by 5 -> ROT18/ROT5\n mirror a<->z ..................... Atbash (D13)\n crib c-p constant ratio .......... affine (lib _fit_affine); constant per position mod k -> Vigenere key = (c-p)\n crib c+p periodic ................ Beaufort; no period but primer then plaintext -> autokey\n crib map consistent, not affine .. keyword substitution (21 letters from crib)\n neighbour keys (Muvr eptl) ....... QWERTY shift;  ;,.' in words -> Dvorak;  ALL printables shift -> ROT47 (D15)/ROT8000\nSAME CHARACTER MULTISET (anagram: one ! , :, slug digits intact) = TRANSPOSITION (D12 reverse, D18 rail 3):\n rail fence (D18: number in prompt = rails; w.rail_solve) | redefence | scytale/columnar (w.col_solve) | route/Caesar box\n | skip k | riffle | word order. Strip only \\r\\n (spaces are ciphertext); accept only text STARTING `Nice work`\nWORDS: Alfa Bravo -> NATO;  -ay endings -> Pig Latin;  N1c3 w0rk -> leet;  Ook./+-<>[] -> esoteric program\nTitle pun -> key: a cipher name + a number/word in the prompt = the key (D18 \"Three rails\"); verify on the crib.\n\"Same ...\"/\"This time ...\" prompt (D20) = yesterday's codec with ONE knob turned (byte/bit order, alphabet, width).\nMastery: line k = day k's codec; keyed/transposed lines restart the key PER LINE (D18 line 18 = 6-8 char rail-3 slug\n tail); D19/D20 lines 19/20 each have their OWN BOM (LE and BE in one blob); D21 line 21 = its own gzip member. STACKS (D16-17, D19-21): output hex/digits/b32/a-p/NUL-rhythm/compressed-magic bytes -> decode AGAIN. Solver: return on the first full slug; slow fallbacks only on a miss.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"compression-family-sweep\", \"concept\": \"other compressors under a text wrapper: zlib (any level byte), raw deflate, bz2, xz, lzma-alone, under base64/base64url/hex/base32/base85/binary\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 = gzip inside std padded base64 ('A familiar wrapper. Something compressed inside.'); D19->D20 showed the lane turns ONE knob the next day, so expect the same wrapper with another squeeze, or the same gzip under another wrapper. Build warmups_codecs.decompress_sweep(t): every wrapper decoder (b64 std/url, padded or not; hex any case/spaced; b32; a85/b85; 8-bit binary) -> magic sniff (1f8b gzip, 78 01/5e/9c/da zlib, BZh bz2, fd377a585a xz, 5d0000 lzma-alone) -> decompress; raw deflate by trial zlib.decompress(b,-15) when no magic. Return the first slug-gated text. Register as a free codec for Mastery fragments (36-char per-fragment members). Fixtures: each compressor x each wrapper, + 6-10 char Mastery fragments. Cost cap < 0.05 s per blob.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"raw-deflate-gzip-quirks\", \"concept\": \"gzip/deflate stream quirks: headerless deflate, truncated CRC trailer, FNAME/FCOMMENT/FEXTRA header fields, multi-member / concatenated gzip\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Knob on D21's codec. gzip.decompress raises on a missing/short trailer and on trailing garbage; use zlib.decompressobj(31) and loop over unused_data for concatenated members; wbits=-15 for raw deflate, 47 for auto zlib/gzip. Header with FNAME (b64 'H4sICA') carries a filename that may hint the next layer -- surface it in the solver's notes, never as the answer. Fixtures: truncated, FNAME/FCOMMENT set, 2-3 concatenated members, mtime != 0, xfl/OS variants.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"decompress-then-redecode\", \"concept\": \"inflated text is another seen codec (gzip of hex/rot13/Morse/b64), or an old free transform over the compressed wrapper (reversed / rot13 / Atbash base64 of gzip)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Stacks a seen family on D21's new one. After every decompress, run decode_chunk + CANDIDATES on the output (depth cap 3, slug gate). Before the b64 magic sniff, also try undoing rev/rot13/Atbash/ROT47 when the text is b64-ish but not valid (rot13 of 'H4sI' = 'U4fV', reversed ends 'Is4H'). Fixtures: gzip(hex(text)), gzip(rot13(text)), rot13(b64(gzip)), rev(b64(gzip)), b64(gzip(b64(text))).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"text-armor-wrappers\", \"concept\": \"text armor wrappers around a body: data: URI, PEM -----BEGIN-----, PGP ASCII armor (=CRC24), MIME part / email (Content-Transfer-Encoding), Intel HEX / Motorola S-record, JSON/XML envelope\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'A familiar wrapper' read literally. Build warmups_codecs.unarmor(t): data:[mime][;base64], PEM/PGP (strip headers, verify CRC24 when present), email.message_from_string (decode each part by its CTE), Intel HEX (:LLAAAATT...CC records, checksum) and S-records -> bytes; then the normal pipeline incl. decompress_sweep. Fixtures: each armor over plain text and over gzip.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"archive-container-in-base64\", \"concept\": \"an archive as the wrapper: zip / tar / tar.gz / 7z / cpio / ar member inside base64 or hex\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'wrapper'/'package'/'bundle' puns. Cue: b64 'UEsDB' (zip), 'N3q8ryc' (7z), gzip that inflates to 'ustar' at offset 257 (tar), '070701' cpio, '!<arch>' ar. Read every member (stored or deflated; try password b'infected' if encrypted), decode each with the pipeline, join in archive order. zipfile/tarfile stdlib; py7zr in .venv (check solver import allowance). Fixtures per container, 1 and 3 members.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"third-party-compressors\", \"concept\": \"non-stdlib compressors: zstd, lz4 frame, brotli, snappy framed, LZO\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Magic: zstd 28b52ffd (b64 'KLUv/'), lz4 frame 04224d18 (b64 'BCJNGA'), snappy framed ff060000734e61507059, brotli has none (trial decode, slug gate). .venv has zstandard, lz4, brotli (+ CLIs in .venv/bin); snappy/LZO need small pure-python decoders. Guard imports (ImportError -> skip) so solvers stay runnable on Homebase. Fixtures under base64 and hex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lzstring-js\", \"concept\": \"LZ-String (JS) compressToBase64 / compressToEncodedURIComponent / compressToUTF16\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"A web-familiar compressor with no magic: base64-alphabet text (URI form uses '+' and '$', no '/') that is not b64-of-a-magic; UTF16 form = dense CJK-range chars. Pure-python decompress (~60 lines, port of pieroxy lz-string), slug-gated. Fixtures for all three forms + Mastery fragments.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"rle-lzw-text-compression\", \"concept\": \"text-level compression: run-length encoding, LZ77 tuples, LZW code lists, Huffman with an included code table\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Keyless 'pressure'/'squeeze' puns without binary bytes. RLE both orders ('3a2b' / 'a3b2', count>=1, digits escaped?); LZ77 '(o,l,c)' tuples; LZW = integer list whose first values are ASCII codes and later ones >= 256 (initial dict 256, also 8-bit+clear-code variants); Huffman: a '{char: bits}' table + bit string. Crib-gated decoders + fixtures.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"middle-endian-pdp\", \"concept\": \"middle-endian / PDP-11 byte order (2143, 3412) for 32-bit words: UTF-32 or u32 char codes\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Retry: attempt 1 FAILED the lib lint ('call __import__() not allowed' in lib/warmups_codecs.py) -- use normal imports. Lower priority now that D21 left the byte-order family, but a 'Same bar' callback stays possible. Hex whose 4-byte words read neither as utf-32-le nor -be: 'N' as UTF-32 in PDP order = 00 00 4e 00. Try all 24 permutations of each 4-byte word, then utf-32-be / utf-16-be, crib-gated; a permuted BOM is the cue.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"byte-family-mastery-cost\", \"concept\": \"Mastery solve time per set as codecs accumulate; lane-solver continuity\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D21 Mastery (103 x 21) died at the 60 s harness budget because solve.py was an ad-hoc generic per-line brute force, not the carried D20 lane solver; restoring the D20 solver + one `_b64z` branch solved 103 sets in 0.34 s (so D20's 18.6 s was not inherent). Rule: copy the previous day's solve.py, add today's codec as one whole-blob step + register_free(name, day, fn), return early, and time hctf solver-test on the real Mastery case before any timed start.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"case-and-digit-loss\", \"concept\": \"case-losing / digit-losing codecs (Morse, NATO, Polybius, tap, Bacon, A1Z26, T9)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Output must be lowercased; A1Z26/Polybius/Bacon/tap have no digit symbols, so slug digits are passed through literally or spelled - the decoder must keep non-alphabet tokens verbatim. Lowercase only the FINAL text, and test a collapsed output for an inner hex/digit layer first (D16 Morse -> UPPERCASE hex, D17 Bacon -> a-p).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"transposition-mastery-joint\", \"concept\": \"short Mastery fragments under a transposition (6-8 chars, key restarts per line)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D18 line 18 ('p-pr5e6' -> 'pper-56') has no charset cue; decode_chunked misses it (a D21 generalize worker's intermediate run left 'Master:i rbsk-...'). Keep the slug-gated per-line rail pass; register any future transposition decoder as a free codec with its day number so _joint_free tries it on each unclaimed line.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"affine-free-strict\", \"concept\": \"affine as a GM-confirmed-ready free codec\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Already prebuilt (wc:affine + SPECULATIVE_FREE + _fit_affine). Risk is only bigram ranking vs rot-N/Atbash in Mastery joint assignment; confirm ratchet path registers it with a day number on first sight.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"chepy-cyberchef-cue\", \"concept\": \"standard-tool fallback for any unseen encoding\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"chepy (venv) has from_base45/58/62/85/91/92/65536, rot_8000, from_upside_down, decode_zero_width, from_fullwidth, from_bacon, from_braille, from_nato, sms_decode_multitap, vigenere_decode, bifid_decode, gzip/zlib/bzip/lzma/lz4/lz77 _decompress, raw_inflate, unzip_all, tar_extract_all; CyberChef ops at tools/npm-cyberchef/node_modules/cyberchef/src/core/operations (Magic recipe finds compression layers).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"base92\", \"concept\": \"base92\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"chepy from_base92 / CyberChef From Base92 decode it; cue = printable minus double-quote and backtick.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"base65536\", \"concept\": \"base65536 / base2048 / base32768\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"chepy from_base65536; others need pip (base2048) - install only if seen.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bifid-adfgvx\", \"concept\": \"Bifid / Trifid / ADFGX / ADFGVX / Nihilist\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"pycipher implements all; key from title; ADFGX cue is the 5/6-letter alphabet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mime-encoded-word\", \"concept\": \"MIME encoded-word headers\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"email.header.decode_header handles =?charset?B|Q?...?=. Body-level MIME wrappers are in text-armor-wrappers.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"esoteric\", \"concept\": \"Brainfuck / Ook! (Chuck Norris unary is prebuilt: chuck_dec)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"No bf interpreter installed; a 20-line stdlib interpreter or pip 'brainfuck-interpreter' if one ever appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"misc-tables\", \"concept\": \"chemical symbols, Cetacean, Citrix CTX1 (DNA/codon, Roman, BCD, Gray, Kenny are prebuilt in warmups_codecs)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Recognition cues only; each is a lookup table the worker can write in one turn; CyberChef has From BCD and Cetacean Cipher Decode.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"homoglyph\", \"concept\": \"homoglyph (Cyrillic/Greek look-alike) substitution\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"unidecode/confusables not installed; NFKC does not fold Cyrillic. Install unidecode only if a day uses it.\"}\n]\n```\nwarmups:address-notation True 1\nwarmups:ap-letter-hex True 1\nwarmups:archive-container-in-base64 True 1\nwarmups:astral-utf16-surrogates True 1\nwarmups:bacon True 1\nwarmups:bacon-hex-lib True 1\nwarmups:base-n-alt-alphabets True 1\nwarmups:base100-emoji True 1\nwarmups:base45 True 1\nwarmups:base62 True 1\nwarmups:base64-utf16le True 1\nwarmups:base91 True 1\nwarmups:baudot True 1\nwarmups:bcd-gray True 1\nwarmups:bifid-std-square True 1\nwarmups:bignum-integer-text True 1\nwarmups:binary-lsb-first True 1\nwarmups:binary-nibbles-hex True 1\nwarmups:bitgroup-base-index True 1\nwarmups:braille True 1\nwarmups:braille-tap-over-hex True 1\nwarmups:byte-add-offset True 1\nwarmups:byte-rotate-bits True 1\nwarmups:charcode-radix True 1\nwarmups:chuck-norris-unary True 1\nwarmups:columnar True 2\nwarmups:compression-family-sweep True 1\nwarmups:crib-polyalpha-key True 1\nwarmups:crib-token-hex True 1\nwarmups:css-color-hex True 1\nwarmups:decompress-then-redecode True 1\nwarmups:dna-acgt True 1\nwarmups:double-columnar-myszkowski True 1\nwarmups:dtmf-keypad True 1\nwarmups:ebcdic-utf16-utf7 True 1\nwarmups:endian-word-swap True 1\nwarmups:free-over-strict True 1\nwarmups:fullwidth-nfkc True 1\nwarmups:fullwidth-unicode True 1\nwarmups:glyph-radix True 1\nwarmups:gsm7-septet-packing True 1\nwarmups:hexdump-formats True 1\nwarmups:iching-hexagram True 1\nwarmups:kenny-ternary True 1\nwarmups:keyboard-layout True 1\nwarmups:keyword-substitution-decode True 1\nwarmups:knob-sweep-prior-codecs True 1\nwarmups:leb128-varint True 1\nwarmups:leetspeak True 1\nwarmups:lzstring-js True 1\nwarmups:middle-endian-pdp True 2\nwarmups:morse-over-codec True 1\nwarmups:morse-plaintext-punct True 1\nwarmups:morse-timing-units True 1\nwarmups:morse-variants True 1\nwarmups:multi-byte-xor True 2\nwarmups:nato-over-hex True 1\nwarmups:nibble-swap-hex True 1\nwarmups:pig-latin True 1\nwarmups:playfair True 1\nwarmups:polybius True 2\nwarmups:punycode True 1\nwarmups:rail-offset T