n decompress/decode | med: knob on D22 (same zlib, different payload) |\n| 155 | yEnc / BinHex 4.0 / Ascii85-with-`<~~>` armor variants | gap (gap yenc-binhex) | yes | `=ybegin line=128 size=..`; `(This file must be converted with BinHex 4.0)` + `:...:` | yEnc: `(b-42-64*esc)%256`; BinHex: RLE90 + hqx (binascii hqx removed in 3.11 -> small decoder) | low-med: retro binary-to-text |\n| 156 | zalgo / combining-mark noise over the sentence (U+0300-036F stacked), or decomposed NFD text | gap (gap zalgo-combining-strip) | yes | letters with many combining diacritics; `unicodedata.combining(c)` > 0 | `''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFD',t) if not unicodedata.combining(c))` | low |\n\"\"\"\nm=re.search(r\"^\\| 145 \\|.*\\n\", s, re.M); s=s[:m.end()]+rows+s[m.end():]\n# cues\nrep(\"\"\" A-Za-z0-9+/ (=), len%4==0 ........ base64 (D1); H4sI = GZIP inside (D21: base64 -d | gzip -dc); eJ zlib, Qlpo bz2,\n                                    /Td6WFo xz, KLUv/ zstd, UEsDB zip, N3q8 7z; bytes binary -> sniff magic, never score\"\"\",\n\"\"\" A-Za-z0-9+/ (=), len%4==0 ........ base64 (D1); H4sI = GZIP inside (D21: base64 -d | gzip -dc); eN = ZLIB 78da (D22:\n   zlib.decompress(b64decode(t)); eJ/eF/eA other levels; zlib = (b0<<8|b1)%31==0, not just 0x78; no magic -> wbits=-15);\n   Qlpo bz2, /Td6WFo xz, KLUv/ zstd, UEsDB zip, N3q8 7z, U2FsdGVkX1 openssl, .eJ flask cookie, eyJ JWT -> never score bytes\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"\"Same ...\"/\"This time ...\" prompt (D20) = yesterday's codec with ONE knob turned (byte/bit order, alphabet, width).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"\"Same ...\"/\"Another ...\"/\"This time ...\" (D20, D22) = yesterday's codec, ONE knob turned (order, alphabet, compressor).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"D21 line 21 = its own gzip member.\"\"\",\"\"\"D21/D22 lines 21/22 = own gzip / zlib streams.\"\"\")\n# gaps json\na=s.index(\"```json\\n\",s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\"))+8; b=s.index(\"\\n```\",a)\ngaps=json.loads(s[a:b]); byid={g['id']:g for g in gaps}\ndrop={'compression-family-sweep','raw-deflate-gzip-quirks','decompress-then-redecode','text-armor-wrappers',\n      'archive-container-in-base64','third-party-compressors','lzstring-js'}\ngaps=[g for g in gaps if g['id'] not in drop]\nbyid['middle-endian-pdp'].update(priority=3, action='note', detail=\"Given up after 2 prebuild attempts (attempt 1 failed the lib lint: '__import__() not allowed'). Byte-order family closed at D20; if a PDP/middle-endian day ever comes: try all 24 permutations of each 4-byte word, then utf-32-be / utf-16-be, crib-gated; a permuted BOM (00 00 fe ff -> fe ff 00 00 ...) is the cue.\")\nbyid['rle-lzw-text-compression'].update(priority=2, detail=byid['rle-lzw-text-compression']['detail']+\" Retry: prebuild attempt 1 did not pass (ok=false); keep the decoders small, stdlib-only, normal imports.\")\nbyid['byte-family-mastery-cost']['detail']=(\"D21 Mastery (103 x 21) died at the 60 s harness budget because solve.py was an ad-hoc generic per-line brute force, not the carried D20 lane solver; the D20 solver + one `_b64z` branch did 0.34 s. D22 Mastery (108 x 22) passed first try with the D21 solver unchanged (plus the solverrt partial-emit wrapper) but solve took 15.9 s and submit 11.8 s -- profile per set if D23 grows it further. Rule: copy the previous day's solve.py, add today's codec as one whole-blob step + register_free(name, day, fn), return early, time hctf solver-test on the real Mastery case before any timed start.\")\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"zlib-header-sweep\",\"concept\":\"zlib header knobs under a text wrapper: smaller-window CMF (08..68), any level byte, FDICT preset dictionary, raw deflate\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Knob on D22 (zlib 78da in base64). The carried D21/D22 solver `_b64z` sniffs zlib by `startswith(b'\\\\x78')` only, so CMF 0x48/0x58/0x68 (b64 'SI'/'WI'/'aI'), FDICT streams and headerless deflate fall through to rot-N garbage. Build warmups_codecs.zlib_any(b): RFC 1950 check (b[0]&15==8, b[0]>>4<=7, (b[0]<<8|b[1])%31==0) -> zlib.decompress; FDICT (b[1]&0x20) -> decompressobj(zdict=...) trying the known crib sentence and the title words; else zlib.decompress(b,-15); else decompressobj(47). Wire it into decode_chunk's base64/hex/b32 branches and as a free codec for 12-24 char Mastery fragments. Fixtures: wbits 9..15 x levels 1/6/9, FDICT with crib dict, raw, each under std/url b64 padded/unpadded and hex.\"},\n {\"id\":\"flask-itsdangerous-cookie\",\"concept\":\"Flask/itsdangerous signed session cookie (.eJ... = zlib payload) and Django signing tokens\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Familiar wrapper' + deflate in the most common web form: '.eJ<b64url zlib>.<ts>.<sig>' (leading dot = compressed), uncompressed 'eyJ...' variant, Django 'eJ...:ts:sig'. Build warmups_codecs.signed_cookie_dec(t): split on '.'/':', urlsafe-b64 re-pad part 0, zlib if dotted, JSON-decode, return the first string value that holds the slug (or the whole JSON text for the slug gate). Fixtures: compressed/uncompressed, with/without timestamp, Mastery fragments (a fragment may be only the '.eJ..' part).\"},\n {\"id\":\"saml-redirect-deflate\",\"concept\":\"URL-encoded base64 of RAW deflate (SAML HTTP-Redirect), optionally inside a query string\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Stacks three seen layers (D7 %XX, D1 base64, D22 deflate) with the zlib header removed. Cues: %2B/%2F/%3D inside b64-ish text, 'SAMLRequest=' / 'data=' keys, b64 that decodes to no magic. Pipeline: parse_qs if '=' and '&' -> unquote (also unquote_plus) -> b64 (std/url, re-pad) -> zlib.decompress(b,-15) / 15 / 31 -> UTF-8 (or XML: take text/attributes holding the slug). Fixtures: raw/zlib/gzip x quoted/unquoted x query/bare.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jwt-jose-segments\",\"concept\":\"JWT/JWS/JWE compact tokens (eyJ...), JWE zip=DEF raw-deflated payload\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Familiar wrapper' and a D11 base64url callback. Split on '.', urlsafe-b64 each part (re-pad), JSON-load header/payload; if header has zip:'DEF' inflate the payload with wbits -15; search every claim string for the slug. Signature is ignored (never needed). Fixtures: alg none/HS256, nested JSON claim, zip:DEF, Mastery fragment = one segment.\"},\n {\"id\":\"pdf-filter-chain\",\"concept\":\"PDF stream filter chains: ASCII85Decode / ASCIIHexDecode / FlateDecode / LZWDecode / RunLengthDecode\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Document-flavoured 'inflate'. Parse '/Filter [...]' (or single name) and apply in order to the bytes between 'stream\\\\r?\\\\n' and 'endstream': base64.a85decode(adobe=True) for '<~..~>', hex until '>', zlib.decompress (+ wbits fallbacks), PDF LZW with early change, RLE (len byte <128 copy, >128 repeat, 128 EOD). Also accept a bare '<~...~>' a85 of zlib. Fixtures: each filter and 2-3 filter chains, with and without the PDF skeleton.\"},\n {\"id\":\"xor-over-compressed-magic\",\"concept\":\"XOR (single/multi-byte) over a compressed/wrapped stream, key recovered from known magic bytes\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Joins the new compression family with a keyed step: after the wrapper decode the bytes show no magic; XOR the first bytes with candidate headers (gzip 1f8b0800000000000203 = 10 known bytes, zlib 78da/789c/7801, zip 504b0304, bz2 425a6839) to get a key, find its period (1..10), decrypt, decompress, slug-gate. Also the reverse order (XOR of the plaintext, then compressed) is already xorkey_solve's job -- route the inflated text into it. Fixtures: key len 1/2/4/8 x gzip/zlib x b64/hex.\"},\n {\"id\":\"openssl-salted-envelope\",\"concept\":\"OpenSSL enc 'Salted__' envelope (U2FsdGVkX1...) with a passphrase from the title/prompt\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"The most 'familiar' encrypted wrapper. Detect b64 'U2FsdGVkX1' / bytes 'Salted__'. Derive key/iv with EVP_BytesToKey (MD5 and SHA-256) and PBKDF2-SHA256 (10000 iters, -pbkdf2 default), ciphers aes-128/192/256-cbc, aes-256-ctr, des-ede3-cbc, rc4; passphrases = every title/prompt word in several cases + 'password'/'infected'/'huntress'. pycryptodome (Crypto) is in .venv -- guard the import. Crib-gated; output may be compressed (run decompress_sweep).\"},\n {\"id\":\"serialization-wrappers\",\"concept\":\"serialization formats as the wrapper: pickle, marshal, msgpack, BSON, CBOR, protobuf wire, Java serialization, PHP serialize, .NET BinaryFormatter\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Wrapper'/'package' puns. NEVER unpickle/deserialize untrusted bytes: use pickletools.genops / a tiny msgpack-CBOR-BSON-protobuf wire walker / regex for PHP 's:N:\\\"...\\\"' and Java TC_STRING (0x74 + u16 len) to pull out strings, then slug-gate (and run decode_chunk on each string). Cues: b64 'gASV'/'gAN' (pickle), 'rO0AB' (Java), 'AAEAAAD/////' (.NET), 0x82-0x8f/0xa0-0xbf leading bytes (msgpack map/str), BSON int32 length + 0x02 type.\"},\n {\"id\":\"inflate-container-headers\",\"concept\":\"inflate-then-header containers: git loose objects (blob N\\\\0), PNG zTXt/iTXt chunks, HTTP chunked + Content-Encoding\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Same zlib as D22 but the inflated bytes carry a container header the slug gate may still find (but a strict 'starts with Nice work' gate would reject). After every decompress strip 'blob|tree|commit <len>\\\\0'; parse PNG chunks and inflate zTXt / compressed iTXt; de-chunk 'Transfer-Encoding: chunked' bodies (hex size lines) then apply Content-Encoding gzip/deflate/br. Fixtures for each.\"},\n {\"id\":\"yenc-binhex\",\"concept\":\"yEnc and BinHex 4.0 binary-to-text encodings\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Retro wrappers. yEnc: '=ybegin ... name=' header, bytes = (c - 42) % 256, '=' escapes subtract 64 more, '=yend size= crc32='. BinHex 4.0: '(This file must be converted with BinHex 4.0)' then ':...:' 6-bit alphabet '!\\\"#$%&'()*+,-012345689@ABCDEFGHIJKLMNPQRSTUVXYZ[`abcdefhijklmpqr', RLE90 (0x90 marker), header + data fork + CRCs; binascii.a2b_hqx is gone in 3.11+, so ship a small decoder.\"},\n {\"id\":\"zalgo-combining-strip\",\"concept\":\"zalgo / combining-mark noise and NFD-decomposed text\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Strip unicodedata.combining() > 0 after NFD; then the normal pipeline. Cue: base letters buried under stacked U+0300-036F marks. Tiny decoder + fixture; register in CANDIDATES.\"}\n]\nprebuild=[g for g in new if g['action']=='prebuild']\ngaps=new[:4]+[g for g in gaps if g['priority']==1]+new[4:9]+[g for g in gaps if g['priority']==2]+new[9:]+[g for g in gaps if g['priority']==3]\nfor g in gaps: assert set(g)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'},g['id']\nids=[g['id'] for g in gaps]; assert len(ids)==len(set(ids))\ns=s[:a]+\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps)+\"\\n]\"+s[b:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(len(gaps), [ (g['id'],g['priority'],g['action']) for g in gaps])\nPYEOF\npython3 -I $TMPDIR/d22an/edit_cov.py","description":"Apply day22 edits to coverage atlas"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":701,"cache_read_input_tokens":82980,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":701},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"79f67d4f-3065-4eed-9a3c-306c83d2fcc2","uuid":"e7036374-a1b1-4491-824b-26589d0f8fd1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:14:25.013Z","request_id":"req_011CgHLLsiNWnQc8oyYWDUGt","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018dcwGBz1ZqRoadcSWFHjz3":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; cat > $TMPDIR/d22an/edit_cov.py <<'PYEOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/warmups.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    n=s.count(old); assert n==1,(n,old[:70]); s=